    },
    {
      "sha": "b69a31092e2eb47c4065b565a3cbb6626418d11c",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/b69a31092e2eb47c4065b565a3cbb6626418d11c",
      "message": "Merge branch 'p1/integration' into p1/ci-reds-a",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-14T04:20:29Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "f0cf9e186353ba4f451e5310153352e3c734337b",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/f0cf9e186353ba4f451e5310153352e3c734337b",
      "message": "Drop the Dockerfile text-match test from the operator compose suite\n\nIt pinned the transport build stage's FROM line by regular expression, and\nthe image now names that stage through a build-image argument. Rendered\ncompose tests keep the transport path the node reads.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-14T04:20:15Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "38edd3b2b15769665d5858d2aa654a418bbf94d4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/38edd3b2b15769665d5858d2aa654a418bbf94d4",
      "message": "Route the MintItemMalformed rejection arm to the mint-item non-canonical family\n\nThe validation machine now emits arm 47, so the typed-reason disposition\ntable must cover it; its non-interactive proof is the mint-item\nnon-canonical category.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-14T04:19:43Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "bf7b3f5a4b35a1874ecc592a66b4e104022f5404",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/bf7b3f5a4b35a1874ecc592a66b4e104022f5404",
      "message": "Give DA committee test fixtures the block_time clock and drop the parent-ledger test\n\nApply validity and signature clocks now count from the state-queue node's\nauthenticated block_time, so the apply-range and submitter fixtures set\nblock_time instead of a header end time, and the stored header records used\nby the peer and libp2p exchange tests carry the raw node datum it is read\nfrom. The parent post-state test pinned the pre-block ledger lookup that\nca44ed805 removed, so it is deleted.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-14T04:19:37Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "2ec6717e173cfad5bb4ddcdb80489d623eef397e",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/2ec6717e173cfad5bb4ddcdb80489d623eef397e",
      "message": "Regenerate the DA deployment fixture on the current blueprint\n\nProduced by the da-deployment-fixture channel sync on a fresh preprod-testing\nblueprint; it picks up the redeemer-canonicity step-02 data and resolved-output\nstep-04 datum contracts.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-14T04:09:14Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "0332d5e959157c652548269e57d87b377d929971",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/0332d5e959157c652548269e57d87b377d929971",
      "message": "Re-take the Q21 and transition-trace descriptor execution ledgers after N2\n\nThe N2 merge (c0d4b8358) is the only merge since the previous re-take that\nchanges on-chain source. Deposit-arm and L2 rows move by a few hundred to\n2,200 mem; fixture-only rows do not move, and no fit judgement, crossing or\nbasis moves. Rows rewritten by each verifier's --update.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-14T03:56:14Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "0f5fd59f5f8ed399a684f8037f8b36f0f607f3f8",
